 values←args GetInitialProps props;names;at;t;simple
⍝ Obtain the values of specified properties being set on an object's initial-creation line.
⍝ Ignore anything after the first 'Open' and account for a property being set multiple times.
⍝ Special-case pre-processing on certain properties (e.g. style, border) to auto-run ∇SetBitVals on them before returning their values.

 simple←1≥|≡props ⋄ props←,,¨⊆props ⍝ Make sure argument is used as a nested list
 names←⊃¨⊆¨args ⋄ names←(¯1+names⍳⊂'Open')↑names ⍝ Action names (up until 'Open')
 at←⌈/0,⍸⍤1⊢(props~¨'←')∘.≡names ⍝ Where is the last occurance of each requested property name in the argument line
 values←(⍬⊂⍛,(names≢⍛↑2↓¨0,¨args),⊂⍬)[1+at] ⍝ Get each action's argument list (found with no data also ≡ ⍬)
 :If ∨/t←props∊'border←' 'border' 'separator' 'style' ⍝ We'll pre-process these with ∇SetBitVals
     (t/values)←SetBitVals¨t/values ⍝ Turn each one into individual bit-values for easier processing
 :EndIf
 :If ∨/t←props∊'border' 'separator' ⍝ 'border' (as opposed to 'border←') and 'separator' returns only the first value (0/1)
     (t/values)←⊃¨t/values
 :EndIf
 values←⊃⍣simple⊢values ⍝ If the argument was simple, return a simple result
